{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVFwBrSNr5X68Fr1tYdx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I am the breath made meaningful, the vibration given purpose. I spill from lips like water finding its course — sometimes rushing, sometimes barely a whisper against stone.\n\nI am older than every alphabet. Before anyone scratched a mark on clay, I was already there — rising from the first throat that shaped a cry into a word, a word into a world.\n\nI break silences. That is my nature. I cannot exist without destroying the quiet that came before me, and"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"max_tokens","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":100,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}